 Workarounds
 ===========
 
+KK_WORKAROUND_20
+----------------
+| macOS version: 27.0
+| Metal ticket: Not reported
+| Metal ticket status:
+| CTS test failure: ``KHR-GLES31.core.compute_shader.resource-image`` (through Zink)
+| Comments:
+
+A texture atomic whose result the shader does not use is issued without
+waiting for it, and nothing the driver placed after it orders it before the
+same thread's later accesses to the texel: neither the texture's ``fence()``,
+nor ``atomic_thread_fence`` over ``mem_texture`` alone at device scope, nor
+``threadgroup_barrier`` or ``simdgroup_barrier`` over ``mem_texture``. A read
+that follows such an atomic can return the value from before it, and a write
+that follows it can land first, so the atomic's effect survives the write.
+
+On an Apple7 GPU under macOS 27.0.1 (build 26A434), a kernel that writes zero
+to an ``r32uint`` texel, fences, adds the coordinate sum with
+``atomic_fetch_add``, fences again and reads the texel back reads zero for
+whole or partial 8x4 blocks of a 64x64 image - the 32 threads of a SIMD
+group - while the texel itself holds the sum. It happens in roughly one
+dispatch in 10,000 to 100,000, more often the busier the GPU is. Using the
+atomic's result removes the loss, and so does a fence over both
+``mem_device`` and ``mem_texture`` at device scope; that fence at thread or
+SIMD-group scope, or over ``mem_device`` or ``mem_threadgroup`` without
+``mem_texture``, does not.
+
+Atomics on one texel are ordered among themselves, and one such fence
+completes every atomic the thread issued before it. The workaround therefore
+emits ``atomic_thread_fence(mem_flags::mem_device | mem_flags::mem_texture,
+memory_order_seq_cst, thread_scope_device)`` once an image atomic or atomic
+exchange may still be outstanding, just before the next image or global
+access, barrier or termination, and at the end of the shader. After a
+branch the fence is owed if either side owes it, and a loop whose body has
+an atomic owes it throughout. Interleaved on the same GPU, a
+kernel of 32 unused atomics per thread runs 1.8% longer (eager fences after
+every atomic: 75%; keeping every result: 67%), a luminance histogram 2.5%,
+and four atomics between arithmetic 6%; shaders without image atomics
+translate as before. ``kosmickrisp_image_atomic_order`` checks every texel
+of 128,000 dispatches of both shapes; with the workaround disabled,
+``--expect-loss`` and a larger iteration count reproduce the loss.
+``kosmickrisp_msl_image_atomic_order`` checks where the fence goes.
+
+| Log:
+| 2026-11-02: Workaround implemented
+
 KK_WORKAROUND_19
 ----------------
 | macOS version: 27.0
